  "body": "## Associated User Story\n\n[P5-40: Allow imported events of any status](https://pt-502.atlassian.net/browse/P5-40)\n\nAs an officer, I want to import GetInvolved events regardless of their source status, so I can choose which valid events to add without changing their status in GetInvolved first.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Officers can preview and select valid events from CSV or Excel files regardless of source status.\n\n- Sunny: An officer uploads a CSV or XLSX containing Approved, Submitted, Initiated, other, or blank source statuses. The preview shows each original status and the import action. The officer chooses valid rows and confirms; only selected rows are imported. Re-importing an event with the same external reference updates that event instead of creating a duplicate.\n- Rainy: A row has missing required data or invalid dates, a file is unreadable or missing required columns, or a regular member attempts an import. Invalid rows show their row-specific errors and cannot be imported; unauthorized users are blocked. Nothing is written during preview, and confirming with no rows selected imports nothing.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Tests pass\n\nLocal validation of this branch:\n\n```text\nbundle exec rspec spec/\n480 examples, 0 failures, 1 pending\n\nnode --test spec/javascript/*.cjs\n8 tests passed, 0 failed\n```\n\nRegression coverage includes mixed statuses, row selection, validation errors, officer/manager access, blocked member/signed-out access, CSV/XLSX parsing, and repeated imports preserving event IDs.\n\n### Rubocop\n\n```text\nbundle exec rubocop\n150 files inspected, no offenses detected\n```\n\n[GitHub Actions for this branch](https://github.com/FA26-CSCE431-software-engineering/PT-502/actions?query=branch%3Ap5-40-import-any-status)\n\n### Manual checks and documentation\n\nChecked the import preview in the browser. Updated the officer guide, troubleshooting, and the import screenshot to explain source statuses and explicit row selection.\n\nNo new dependencies, database migrations, or deployment configuration changes are required.\n\n## Section D: Deferred items / exclusions\n\n- Non-author code review and the human-only maintainability checks remain for the reviewer. GitHub CI results are available at the link above.\n- The RSpec pending example already existed before this change.\n- No new RuboCop exclusions were added.\n",
